# Thin Shell — Dual-SOT derivation spike

Phase **4bu** locks the dual-SOT inventory and derivation **rules** without emitting capability codegen yet.

Until derivation lands, packages **must dual-publish**: manifest packaging keys stay for API/admission/codegen; shell runtime enablement comes only from `plugin.capabilities.*`.

## Layers (unchanged covenant)

| Layer | Role |
| --- | --- |
| **Shell runtime SOT** | `plugin.capabilities.*` after plugin load / warm |
| **Package packaging** | `workspace.manifest.json` keys — API, admission, legacy codegen |

**Rule:** declaring a packaging enablement flag that formerly drove a deleted web binder requires the matching capability in the **same** change. Manifest alone does not admit shell behavior.

## Dual-SOT inventory (shell-facing)

Pairs where packaging and capability must stay aligned:

| Manifest signal | Capability slot | Shape check (spike) | Exemplars |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `wizardCreate.extendedChrome === true` | `wizardCreate` | `extendedChrome === true` | denali |
| `workspaceFinance.supported === true` | `financeNav` | `supported === true` | denali, finance-ws5 |
| `workspaceFinance.capabilities.ops === true` **or** `workspaceFinance.opsManifest` present | `financeOps` | `typeof resolveManifest === "function"` | denali, finance-ws5 |
| `workspaceBooking.opsManifest` present | `bookingOps` | `typeof resolveManifest === "function"` | denali, booking-ws2 |
| `operatorShell.phase3NavLinks` non-empty | `operatorShellNav` | `links.length === phase3NavLinks.length` | urban |

**Out of scope for derivation (not dual-SOT packaging gates):** Pattern B `ensureReady` UI surfaces, draftShell/chrome bags, opaque §2.4 loaders/media/i18n allowlist.

## Derivation rules (future codegen contract)

When Architect scopes codegen, emit **stubs only** for rows above:

1. Read `workspace.manifest.json`.
2. For each row whose manifest signal is true, ensure the plugin factory publishes the capability with the shape check.
3. Do **not** delete packaging keys in the same slice as first derivation — API/admission may still consume them.
4. Prefer pure Pattern A stubs (`{ supported: true }`, `{ resolveManifest }`, `{ links }`, `{ extendedChrome: true }`). Never put React on derived stubs.

```text
manifest signal true
        │
        ▼
codegen / helper asserts capability present
        │
        ▼
plugin.capabilities.<slot>  == shell runtime SOT
```

## Spike boundaries (4bu)

| In | Out |
| --- | --- |
| Inventory doc + arch consistency tests | Full codegen of capability stubs |
| Freeze derivation **rules** | Dropping manifest keys |
| Prove denali / finance-ws5 / booking-ws2 / urban / negatives | Rewriting plugin factories to “derive-only” |

